$DATUM Procedure D: Aldol reaction between 2,2,2-trifluoroacetophenone dm) and
1-phenyl-l-(trimethvlsilvoxy)ethylene (7): To 2, 2,
2-Trifluoroacetophenone (0.53 g, 3.0 mmol) in a dry flask under N2 were
added THF (anhydrous, 15 mL) and l-phenyl-l-(trimethylsilyoxy)ethylene
(0.75 mL, 3.60 mmol based on 98% purity). The solution was cooled to -30
°C and carbene 5 (5 mg, 0.014 mmol) was added in one portion. The mixture
was stirred at 0 °C for 65 h. HC1 aq solution (1 N, 3 mL) was added and
most of the solvent evaporated under vacuum. Methanol (15 mL) and HC1 aq
solution (1 N, 3 mL) was added and the solution was stirred at 23 °C for
70 h. Saturated NaHCO3 solution (3 mL) and water (3 mL) were added. Most
of the solvents were evaporated under vacuum and dichloromethane (60 mL)
was added and the aqueous layer was extracted with dichloromethane (30
mL). Organic layers were combined and solvents were removed under vacuum
to give the crude residue, which was purified by silica gel flash
chromatography (5% ethyl acetate/hexanes) to give pure product 8m as a
colorless oil (0.84 g, 95% yield). 1H NMR (CDCI3, 400 MHz) δ 7.93-7.91
(m, 2H), 7.63-7.59 (m, 3H), 7.49-7.45 (m, 2H), 7.37-7.29 (m, 3H), 5.70
(s, 1 H), 4.04 (d, J = 17.3 Hz, 1H), 3.64 (d, J = 17.4 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR
(C6D6, 100 MHz) δ 199.8, 138.4, 136.6, 134.1, 128.81, 128.78, 128.6,
128.4, 126.8, 125.5 (q, J C-F = 283 Hz), 76.9(q, J C-F = 28Hz),40.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene-Catalyzed Mukaiyama Aldol Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
