$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the asymmetric Mukaiyama-Type Aldol Reaction: A
flame-dried Schlenk tube under argon atmosphere was charged with Cu(OTf)2
(0.025 mmol) and sulfoximine 4 (0.026 mmol). Then, dry toluene (1.5 mL)
was added, and the resulting deep green solution was stirred for 30 min
at room temperature. The reaction mixture was cooled to reaction
temperature. Subsequently, pyruvate ester 5 (0.25 mmol), enol silyl ether
6 (0.30 mmol), and 2,2,2-trifluoroethanol (0.30 mmol) were added. After
stirring for the indicated period of time, the solvent was removed, and
the product was purified by flash chromatography (PE:Et2O˜1:1). The
absolute configurations of 7a was determined by measuring HPLC and
compared to the literature values5 of the corresponding enantiomers. By
using (S,S)-4, the (R)-configurated product 7a was formed in preference.
For the other products it was assigned in analogy.
(R)-Methyl-(2-hydroxy-2-methyl-4-oxo-4-phenyl)-butanoate (7a). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.52 (s, 3H), 3.36 (d, J = 17.6 Hz, 1H), 3.67 (d, J
= 17.9 Hz, 1H), 3.78 (s, 3H), 7.47-7.49 (m, 2H), 7.57-7.61 (m, 1H),
7.94-7.97 (m, 2H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 26.4, 47.9, 52.7,
72.6, 128.0, 128.5, 133.5, 136.1, 176.2, 198.6 ppm. The enantiomer ratio
was determined by HPLC analysis using a Chiralcel ODH column (flow rate
0.9 mL/min, heptane/i-PrOH: 95/5, λ = 254 nm, 25 °C); tr(R) = 16.0 min,
tr(S) = 19.4 min; 94% ee (R).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 94% ee, reaction at rt gave similar yield but slightly
lower stereoselectivity, optimization study, optimized on chiral ligand
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM C1-Symmetric Oxazolinyl Sulfoximines as Ligands in Copper-Catalyzed
Asymmetric Mukaiyama Aldol Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sedelmeier, Joerg; Hammerer, Tim; Bolm, Carsten
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(5), 917-920

