$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1) Aldol reaction of aldehyde 2s and Brassard's diene 1. To 2 mL THF
solution of freshly prepared (R)-BTHL, the aldehyde 2s (0.5 mmol) and
Brassard's diene 1 (220 mg, 1 mmol) was added successively. After
stirring for 4 h at room temperature, the reaction solution was cooled to
0 °C and quenched with five drops of 1M HCl. After stirring for
additional 15 min, the mixture was neutralized with saturated NaHCO3.
After usual workup, the residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel to afford the aldol product 5. Colorless liquid, yield 95%. [α
]D 27 = - 4.90 (c 1.30, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 6.36 (dd, J
= 19.1, 1.3, 1H), 6.12 (dd, J = 19.1, 5.2 Hz, 1H), 5.22 (s, 1H), 4.36
(dd, J = 5.1, 4.0 Hz, 1H), 4.09 (s, 3H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 2.65-2.50 (m, 1H),
2.28 (brs, 1H), 1.75-1.52 (m, 6H), 1.45 (dd, J = 14.8, 7.3 Hz, 6H), 1.27
(d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 1.15-0.91 (m, 15H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ
165.77, 148.26, 129.26, 96.24, 76.52, 61.15, 51.05, 46.24, 29.18, 27.36,
13.78, 13.21, 9.60; ESI-HRMS: (M+Na)+, calcd. for C22H42O4NaSn: 513.2003,
found: 513.2010.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly Enantio- and Diastereoselective Vinylogous Aldol Reaction by
LiCl-Assisted BINOL-Titanium Species
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Guowei; Wang, Baomin; Qi, Shuai; Zhao, Jinfeng; Zhou, Yuhan; Qu,
Jingping
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(11), 2734-2737

