$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the asymmetric
Mukaiyama-Type Aldol Reaction: A flame-dried Schlenk tube under argon
atmosphere was charged with Cu(OTf)2 (0.025 mmol) and sulfoximine 4
(0.026 mmol). Then, dry toluene (1.5 mL) was added, and the resulting
deep green solution was stirred for 30 min at room temperature. The
reaction mixture was cooled to reaction temperature. Subsequently,
pyruvate ester 5 (0.25 mmol), enol silyl ether 6 (0.30 mmol), and
2,2,2-trifluoroethanol (0.30 mmol) were added. After stirring for the
indicated period of time, the solvent was removed, and the product was
purified by flash chromatography (PE:Et2O˜1:1). The absolute
configurations of 7a was determined by measuring HPLC and compared to the
literature values5 of the corresponding enantiomers. By using (S,S)-4,
the (R)-configurated product 7a was formed in preference. For the other
products it was assigned in analogy.
(1’S,4R)-4-(1’-Hydroxy-1’-methoxycarbonylethyl)-5-oxacyclopent-2-enone
(9)7: The product was prepared according to the general procedure. It was
obtained in 95% yield after flash chromatography. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 1.52 (s, 3H), 3.84 (s, 3H), 5.13 (t, J= 2.0 Hz, 1H),
6.22-6.25 (m, 1H), 7.38-7.42 (m, 1H) ppm; 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
21.5, 53.4, 75.1, 86.0, 123.3, 152.3, 172.3, 173.5 ppm. The enantiomer
ratio was determined by HPLC analysis using a Chiralcel AD column (flow
rate 1.0 mL/min, heptane/i-PrOH: 90/10, λ = 254 nm, 20 °C; tr = 13.9 min
[(1’S,4R), anti, major], tr = 15.4 min [(1’R,4S), anti, minor]; 98% de,
22% ee.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 98% de, 22% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM C1-Symmetric Oxazolinyl Sulfoximines as Ligands in Copper-Catalyzed
Asymmetric Mukaiyama Aldol Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sedelmeier, Joerg; Hammerer, Tim; Bolm, Carsten
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(5), 917-920

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME68 STEP1
