$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.2. Diastereoselective Mukaiyama aldol
reaction of cyclohexanones with acyclic ketene acetals Ethyl
(1-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)cyclohexyl)acetate (4a) Ethyl
((1S*,2S*)-1-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2-methylcyclohexyl)acetate (4b)
According to the synthetic procedure for 4a, this compound was obtained
in 94% yield (295.3 mg, 0.94 mmol) by the reaction of
2-methylcyclohexanone 2b (121 μL, 1.0 mmol) with
tert-butyl(1-ethoxyvinyloxy)dimethylsilane (303.1 mg, 1.5 mmol) in CH2Cl2
(2.0 mL) in the presence of Tf2CHCH2CHTf2 1 (0.29 mg, 0.5 μmol) for 2.5 h
at -178 °C. Colorless oil;. IR (neat) ν 2932, 2857, 1736, 1061, 1040,
835, 772 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.08 (3H, s), 0.10 (3H, s),
0.87-0.93 (3H, m), 0.89 (9H, s), 1.18 (1H, qt, J = 12.8, 3.9 Hz), 1.24
(3H, t, J = 7.1 Hz), 1.27-1.78 (8H, m), 2.35 (1H, d, J = 12.8 Hz), 2.77
(1H, d, J = 12.8 Hz), 4.03-4.16 (2H, m); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ -12.2
and -11.8, 14.2, 15.6, 18.8, 21.8, 25.9, 26.0, 30.5, 37.7, 38.8, 46.4,
60.1, 76.3, 170.8; MS (ESI-TOF) m/z 337 [M+Na]+; HRMS calcd for
C17H34NaO3Si [M+Na]+, 337.2175; found, 337.2184.
