$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the Vinylogous Aldol
reaction of Brassard's diene 1 and aldehydes: Under Ar atmosphere in a
dry Schlenk tube, a mixture of Ti(OiPr)4 (0.4 mmol) and (R)-BINOL (0.4
mmol) was stirred in THF (8 mL) at room temperature for 20 min. Then to
this mixture was added H2O (7.2 μL, 0.4 mmol) with a syringe. After
another 20 min, anhydrous LiCl (18 mg, 0.4 mmol) kept in a Schlenk tube
was quickly added bottle to bottle under Ar atosphere. After stirring for
30 min, 2 mL of the catalyst solution was transferred to another Schlenk
tube and the aldehyde (0.5 mmol) and Brassard's diene 1 (220 mg, 1 mmol)
were added successively. After stirring for indicated time at room
temperature, the reaction solution was cooled to 0 °C and quenched with
five drops of 1M HCl. After stirring for additional 15 min, the mixture
was neutralized with saturated aqueous NaHCO3. After usual workup, the
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel to afford the
aldol product. (4R,5R,Z)-methyl
5-(4-chlorophenyl)-5-hydroxy-3-methoxy-4-methylpent-2-enoate (3g): This
product was obtained as a colorless oil in 94% yield after column
chromatography (acetone/petroleum ether = 1/12). [α ] D 22 = -35.3 (c
0.60, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.30 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.25
(d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 4.99 (s, 1H), 4.83 (dd, J = 4.9, 3.1 Hz, 1H), 3.87
(s, 3H), 3.63 (s, 3H), 2.62-2.46 (m, 1H), 1.79 (s, 1H), 1.09 (d, J = 6.9
Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.37, 165.74, 141.04, 133.32,
128.51, 127.59, 96.29, 74.92, 61.47, 51.23, 48.30, 12.92; ESI-HRMS:
(M+Na)+, calcd. for C14H17ClO4Na: 307.0713, found: 307.0703;
Diastereomeric ratio and enantiomeric excess were determined to be >98:<2
and >98% respectively (determined by HPLC using chiral OJ-H column,
hexane/2-propanol = 9/1, λ = 254 nm, 30 °C, 0.7 mL/min, (syn) tmajor =
16.4 min, tminor = 15.9 min, (anti) t = 15.9 min, t = 18.6 min).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
