$DATUM Ethyl ester 94. In an inert atmosphere box,
(R,R)-diethylbis(indanaoxazoline) (375 mg, 0.969 mmol) and Sn(OTf)2 (367
mg, 0.881 mmol) were added to a flask that was fitted with a serum cap,
removed from the inert atmosphere box and charged with CH2Cl2 (17.6 mL).
The resulting suspension was stirred for 1 h to give a colorless
solution. The solution of catalyst 93 was cooled to −78 °C and
siloxyfuran 90 (1.5 g, 8.81 mmol) was added followed by distilled ethyl
glyoxylate-toluene solution (1.18 mL, 13.2 mmol). The resulting solution
was stirred at −78 °C for 30 min and filtered through a plug of silica
gel with Et2O (50 mL). Concentration of the ether solution gave the crude
silyl ether that was dissolved in EtOAc (40 mL) and 1N HCl (2 mL). After
stirring for 1 h, this solution was poured into a separatory funnel and
diluted with CH2Cl2 (150 mL) and sat. aq. NaHCO3 (40 mL). The layers were
seperated and the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2. The collected
organic layers were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated. Purification by flash chromatography (50% EtOAc/hexanes)
provided ethyl ester 94 (1.65 g, 94%, d.r. > 50:1, 95% ee) as a clear
colorless oil that was homogeneous by both NMR and TLC Product ratios
were determined by HPLC (Chiralcel AD column, 6% isopropanol in hexanes,
flow 0.7 mL/min): anti- (2R,3R) enantiomer tr = 31.83 min, anti-(2S,3S)
enantiomer tr = 35.92 min; syn enantiomers tr = 45.91, 67.34 min; [α]D
−90.3 (c 1.18, CHCl3); IR (neat) 3448, 2985, 2931, 1756, 1748, 1246,
1205, 1063 cm−1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.97 (dq, 1H, J = 1.4, 0.5
Hz), 5.15 (ddd, 1H, J = 6, 2, 0.4 Hz,), 4.48 (dd, 1H, J = 7, 4 Hz, 1H),
4.29 (dq, 1H, J = 11, 7 Hz), 4.27 (dq, 1H, J = 11, 7 Hz), 3.11 (d, 1H, J
= 7 Hz), 1.93 (dt, 3H, J = 2, 1 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) d 173.4,
170.6, 143.8, 132.3, 81.1, 70.6, 62.5, 14.1, 10.7; Exact mass calcd for
C9H12O5 [M + NH4]+ 218.1029; found 218.1039 (CI).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, greater than 50:1 d.r., in-situ generated catalyst, 95%
ee
