$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the aldol reaction To a stirred solution of the
aldehyde 1c (130 mg, 236 μmol) in freshly distilled CH2Cl2 (5 mL) cooled
to -60 °C was added the BF3.OEt2 (90 μL, 710 μmol) with a syringe. After
5 min 7 (102 μL, 472 μmol) was added and the mixture stirred at -60 °C
for 18h. The reaction was quenched with saturated NaHCO3 (5 mL) and
extracted with CH2Cl2 (3x10 mL). The combined organic phases were dried
(MgSO4), filtered and evaporated to give a colorless oil. The
diastereomeric ratio was determined by 1H NMR on the crude reaction
mixture. Flash chromatography of the residue (pentane:EtOAc 20:1) yielded
3b (141 mg, 92%) as a colorless oil.
N-{(1R*,2S*)-1-[(S*)-(tert-Butyl-dimethyl-silanyloxy)-cyclohexyl-methyl]-2-hydroxy-5,5-
dimethyl-4-oxo-hexyl}-4-methyl-benzenesulfonamide (3b) 1H NMR (CDCl3,
400MHz) δ 7.75 (d, J = 8.2, 2H), 7.31 (d, J = 8.2, 2H), 5.13 (d, J = 8.9
Hz, 1H), 4.51 (t, J = 3.5 Hz, 1H), 3.60 (dd, J = 7.4, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 3.48
(s, 1H), 3.41 (dd, J = 8.9, 2.3 Hz, 1H), 2.53 (dd, J = 18.0, 6.3 Hz, 1H),
2.42 (s, 3H), 2.19 (dd, J = 18.0, 6.1 Hz, 1H), 1.76-0.89 (m, 29H), 0.16
(s, 3H), 0.04 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100MHz) δ 214.4, 143.4, 138.4,
129.8, 127.0, 82.4, 66.3, 64.8, 56.0, 44.0, 41.4, 40.1, 29.4, 29.3, 26.9,
26.3, 26.2, 26.1, 26.0, 25.8, 21.4, 18.3, -3.5, -4.5; IR (neat) 3400,
2930, 1700 cm-1; HRMS (FAB+) calcd for C28H50NO5SSi (M+H): 540.3179,
found: 540.3179.
