$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparations of 9c 9c: To a solution of butyraldehyde (14.4 mg, 0.20
mmol) and 4b (32.2 mg, 0.10 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1.5 mL) at -78 °C was added
TiCl4 (11.0 μL, 0.10 mmol). After stirring at -78 °C for 2 h, the
reaction was warmed to 0 °C for 30 min before quenched with sat aq NH4Cl
(4 mL) and extracted with Et2O (3 × 5 mL). Combined organic extracts were
dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated under reduced pressure.
Purification of the crude residue via silica gel flash column
chromatography (gradient eluent: 0-2% of EtOAc/petroleum ether) afforded
9c. Colorless oil, yield (22 mg, 93%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.92 (t,
3H, J = 7.2 Hz), 1.42-1.61 (m, 4H), 2.02 (s, 3H), 3.10 (s, 1H), 4.07 (d,
1H, J = 8.0 Hz), 4.10-4.17 (m, 1H), 7.49 (t, 2H, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.60 (t,
1H, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.99 (d, 2H, J = 7.6 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
12.0, 14.0, 19.2, 36.5, 52.3, 67.8, 128.4, 128.7, 133.5, 135.7, 194.9; IR
(neat) cm-1 3469s, 3060w, 2958s, 2923s, 2867m, 1657s, 1595m, 1578m,
1447m, 1392m, 1360m, 1298s, 1229s, 1209s, 1127m, 1077s, 1030m, 1000m,
852w, 820m; HRMS (MALDI, m/z) calcd for C13H18O2SNa (M+Na)+: 261.0920,
found 261.0921.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama aldol reaction
