$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reagents: benzaldehyde (75 mg, 0.71 mmol), 2-(trimethylsilyloxy)furan 2a
(133 mg, 0.85 mmol), and Bi(OTf)3•4H2O (5.0 mg, 0.007 mmol). The reaction
was stirred for 0.5 h at -78 °C and . The reaction was diluted with
tetrahydrofuran (1.0 mL) and quenched with 10% aqueous HCl (1.0 mL). The
mixture was stirred for 0.25 h at room temperature, neutralized by
addition of a saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution, and extracted with ethyl
acetate. The organic phases were combined, dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated under reduced pressure (rotary evaporator). The syn/anti
ratio (94:6) was determined by 1H NMR analysis of the crude product (δ
major: 4.71 ppm, δ minor: 5.10 ppm). The crude product was then purified
on silica gel (25% ethyl acetate/hexane) to afford 122 mg (91%) of 3a as
two separated diastereoisomers: Syn diastereoisomer. mp 57 °C (white
solid); Rf = 0.26 (30% ethyl acetate/hexane); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
= 7.36–7.42 (m, 5H), 7.18 (dd, J = 5.8, 1.6 Hz, 1H) 6.13 (dd, J = 5.8,
2.0 Hz, 1H), 5.17 (dt, J = 7.1, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 4.71 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 1H),
2.73 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 172.6, 153.2, 137.9,
129.2, 129.1, 126.9, 123.3, 87.1, 76.0; IR (film): 3438, 1764 cm-1. Anti
diastereoisomer: Rf = 0.28 (30% ethyl acetate/hexane); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 7.34–7.42 (m, 6H), 6.20 (dd, J = 5.8, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 5.19 (dt,
J = 3.6, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 5.10(t, J = 4.2 Hz, 1H), 2.45 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 173.2, 152.9, 139.1, 129.0, 128.8, 126.3, 123.5,
86.7, 73.4. IR (film): 3438, 1764 cm–1, 1764 cm-1. Anti diastereoisomer:
Rf = 0.28 (30% ethyl acetate/hexane); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
7.34–7.42 (m, 6H), 6.20 (dd, J = 5.8, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 5.19 (dt, J = 3.6, 1.8
Hz, 1H), 5.10 (t, J = 4.2 Hz, 1H), 2.45 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 173.2, 152.9, 139.1, 129.0, 128.8, 126.3, 123.5, 86.7, 73.4.
IR (film): 3438, 1764 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (isomer mix.), yield depends on reaction conditions
(solvent and amt. of cat.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diastereoselective Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction of 2-(Trimethylsilyloxy)furan
Catalyzed by Bismuth Triflate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ollevier, Thierry; Bouchard, Jean-Emmanuel; Desyroy, Valerie
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(1), 331-334

