zinc(II) trifluoromethanesulfonate (9 mg, 0.025 mmol, 10 mol%) in
EtOH/H2O (9/1) 1.0 mL was stirred at -20 °C (15-20 min.). To the
resulting homogeneous solution silyl enol ether 5 (115 μL, 0.5 mmol, 2
equivalents) and appropriate aldehyde (0.25 mmol) were added and
resulting homogeneous solution was left in refrigerator at -20 °C
overnight without stirring. The reaction mixture was poured onto silica
gel column and eluted by AcOEt/hexane (1:4) to yield desired aldols.
(2S,3S)-3-Hydroxy-2-methyl-1,3-diphenyl-propan-1-one (7a). 1H NMR (200
MHz) δ (syn): 1.19 (d, 3H, J 7.2 Hz), 3.67 (d, 1H, OH, J 1.7 Hz), 4.11
(dq, 1H, J 3.0, 7.3 Hz), 5.23 (brs, 1H), 7.20 - 7.65 (m, 8H), 7.85-8.20
(m, 2H). 13C NMR (50 MHz) δ: 11.1, 47.1, 73.0, 125.9, 127.3, 128.2,
128.4, 128.7, 133.5, 135.6, 141.7, 205.8. [α]D +3.5 (c 0.1 in CHCl3, 85%
ee), lit.[4] for syn-(2S,3S)-5a: [α]D +11.7 (c 1.03 in CHCl3, 95% ee);
HPLC (Daicel Chiralpak AD-H, hexane/i-PrOH = 9/1, flow rate = 1 mL/min;
syn isomer: t1 = 9.9 min, t2 = 12.2 min (major), anti isomer: t1 = 14.6
min, t2 = 16.0 min.
