$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure for the Catalytic
Asymmetric Vinylogous Mukaiyama Aldol Addition: Preparation of
(E)-(R)-8-(tert-butyl-diphenylsilanyloxy)-
5-hydroxy-2-methyl-oct-2-enethioic acid S-tert-butyl ester SI13. The
crude reaction mixture was obtained by following the general procedure
for the catalytic asymmetric vinylogous Mukaiyama aldol addition using
aldehyde SI12 (243 mg, 0.745 mmol, 1.00 eq) as starting material and was
purified by flash chromatography using a 2.5 × 18 cm silica gel column
eluting with a solvent mixture of 5% acetone/hexanes (700 mL). The eluant
was collected in 30 mL portions and the product containing fractions (9
to 20) were combined and concentrated to give alcohol SI13 (342 mg, 0.686
mmol, 92%) as a clear colorless oil. The ratio of enantiomers was
determined to be er = 95:5 (with BF3•EtO2 as Lewis-acid er = 50:50) by
HPLC analysis using a Daicel Chiralcel OD-H silica column, eluting with a
mobile phase of 5% 2-propanol/hexanes and a flow rate of 0.5 mL/min,
which gave the retention times for the major and minor enantiomers of
17.8 and 20.2 min, respectively, detecting with a Rainin Dynamax
Refractive Index Detector Model RI-1: Rf 0.41 (25% EtOAc/hexanes); [α]D
20 +0.9 (c = 1.030, CHCl3); 500 MHz 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.69 – 7.67 (m, 4H),
7.46 – 7.39 (m, 6H), 6.75 (ddq, J = 7.3, 7.3, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 3.81 (dddd, J
= 12.0, 6.0, 3.0, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 3.73 – 3.69 (m, 2H), 2.47 (bs, 1H), 2.43 –
2.33 (m, 2H), 1.86 (s, 3H), 1.74 – 1.65 (m, 4H), 1.51 (s, 9H), 1.07 (s,
9H); 125 MHz 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 195.0, 139.0, 135.8 (5), 133.7 (2), 129.9
(2), 127.9 (4), 71.0, 64.3, 47.6, 36.9, 34.4, 30.1 (3), 29.0, 27.1 (3),
19.4, 12.8; 125 MHz DEPT (CDCl3) δ CH3: 30.1 (3), 27.0 (3), 12.8. CH2:
64.3, 36.9, 34.4, 29.0. CH: 135.8, 135.8 (4), 129.9 (2), 127.9 (4), 71.0.
C: 195.0, 139.0, 133.7 (2), 47.6, 19.4; IR (neat) 3424 (bs), 3070, 3044,
2997, 2951, 2930, 2858, 1964, 1894, 1822, 1650, 1589, 1473, 1455, 1428,
1389, 1362, 1305, 1186, 1161, 1112, 1029, 1007, 936, 899, 823, 794, 741,
702, 688, 662, 614 cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C29H42O3SSi: C, 69.83; H, 8.5.
Found: C, 69.78; H, 8.51
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 4A mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Catalytic Asymmetric Vinylogous Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Heumann, Lars V.; Keck, Gary E.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(21), 4275-4278

