$DATUM Methyl
3-trimethylsilyloxy-2,2,4-trimethyl-7-tributylstannanyl-hepta-4,6-dienoate
(8a). To a solution of the freshly prepared catalyst (S)-1c (0.296 mmol,
20 mol%) at -40°C were successively added a solution of triphenylphospine
oxide (0.171 g, 0.616 mmol, 0.5 equiv) in toluene (2 mL) and aldehyde
E,E-7 (0.475 g, 1.23 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in 0.5 mL of toluene. After 15 min
stirring at -40°C, (1-methoxy-2-methyl-propenyloxy)-trimethylsilane (300
μL, 1.47 mmol, 1.2 equiv) was added slowly for 20 min to the reaction.
The mixture was stored at -40°C for 20 h and then quenched with saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 solution (2 mL), washed with H2O (10 mL) and extracted
with ethyl acetate (3 × 20 mL). The combined organic phase was washed
with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated under vacuum
provided the crude product as yellow oil. Purification of the crude
product by flash chromatography (Et 2 O/hexane, v/v, 1/10) to afford
compound 8a (0.632 g, 92 % yield) as yellow oil. IR (neat): νmax 2956,
2925, 2872, 2853, 1741, 1730, 1463, 1250, 1134, 1070, 885; 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.70 (dd, 1H, J1 = 18.6 Hz, J2 = 10.2 Hz), 6.18 (d, 1H, J
= 18.6 Hz); 5.91 (d, 1H, J = 9.9 Hz); 4.30 (s, 1H); 3.63 (s, 3H); 1.74
(s, 3H); 1.58-1.42 (m, 6H); 1.38-1.22 (m, 6H); 1.14 (s, 3H);1.06 (s, 3H);
0.94-0.80 (m, 15H); 0.03-0.01 (br s, 9H) (13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ
177.6, 142.6, 135.8, 134.3, 131.7, 82.1, 51.8, 49.5, 29.3, 27.5, 22.0,
20.9, 14.3, 13.9, 9.7, 0.1.
