$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure of the TFSI-H
catalyzed Mukaiyama cross-aldol reaction: To a solution of 11 (851 mg,
5.00 mmol) and 2,2-dimethoxypropane (624 mg, 6.00 mmol) in CH2Cl2 at -78
°C, was added dropwise TFSI-H (500 L, 0.5 M solution in CH2Cl2, 0.025
mmol, 5 mol%). After 30 min at -78 °C, the reaction mixture was poured
into a sat. aq solution of NaHCO3 and extracted with ether. The combined
extracts were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel (Cyclohexane/EtOAc: 90/10) to give
20.18b Compound 24, yield 92%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mukaiyama cross-aldol reaction, product depends on reaction
conditions-stoichiometry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Carbon-carbon bond forming reactions by using
bistrifluoromethanesulfonimide
