$DATUM (R)-4-benzyl-3-((4R,5R,E)-7,7-dibromo-5-hydroxy-2,4-dimethylhepta-2,6-dienoyl)oxazolidin-2-one
(12). To a solution of aldehyde 11 (2.68 g, 12.5 mmol) in DCM (34 mL) at
-78 °C was added freshly distilled TiCl4 (2M in DCM, 3.12 mL, 6.24 mmol)
dropwise, followed by a solution of silyl N,O-acetal 9 (2.42 g, 6.24
mmol) in DCM (34 mL). The reaction mixture was left to stand for 18 h at
-20 °C, before being quenched with pyridine (5 mL), Na+/K+ tartrate (15
mL) and NaHCO3 (15 mL), and the mixture was stirred at room temperature
until a homogeneous solution was obtained. This mixture was extracted
with EtOAc (3 × 15 mL), and the combined extracts were dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography (1:10 to 1:2
EtOAc/pet. ether) afforded the vinylogous aldol adduct 12 (2.80 g, 5.74
mmol, 92%, 10:1 anti:syn) as a yellow solid. Recrystallization (DCM/Et2O)
then provided diastereomerically pure 12 as a white solid. Rf 0.30 (1:2
EtOAc/pet. ether); m.p. = 145-147 °C; [α]20D = -4.8 (c 0.50, CHCl3); IR
(thin film) νmax = 3485 (br), 2968, 2929, 1772, 1683; 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δH 7.33 (2H, m, ArH), 7.25 (1H, m, ArH), 7.20 (2H, d, J = 7.5 Hz,
ArH), 6.51 (1H, d, J = 8.7 Hz, H12), 5.75 (1H, d, J = 10.3 Hz, H9), 4.82
(1H, m, NCH), 4.31 (1H, t, J = 8.8 Hz, OCH2aCH), 4.19 (1H, dd, J = 8.8,
6.4 Hz, OCH2bCH), 4.10 (1H, ddd, J = 8.4, 8.2, 3.4 Hz, H11), 3.32 (1H,
dd, J = 13.6, 3.4 Hz, CH2aAr), 3.23 (1H, d, J = 3.4 Hz, OH), 2.88 (1H,
dd, J = 13.6, 9.1 Hz, CH2bAr), 2.71 (1H, m, H10), 1.97 (3H, s, Me8), 1.06
(3H, d, J = 6.8 Hz, Me10); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δC 171.2, 154.1,
140.0, 138.9, 134.7, 132.3, 129.5, 129.0, 127.5, 92.2, 76.3, 66.4, 55.0,
39.8, 37.6, 15.7, 14.0; HRMS (ES+) calcd for C19H21NO479Br2Na [M+Na]+
507.9735, found 507.9760. Crystal system Orthorhombic; Space group
P2(1)2(1)2(1); a = 6.3289(1)≈ b = 10.5900(2)≈ c = 30.2364(7)≈ α = 90∞ β =
90∞ γ = 90∞ Z = 4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, vinylogous Mukaiyama aldol reaction, key step
