$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Mukaiyama Aldol Reactions Reported in Tables 1
and 2. Preparation of ent-9. To a cold (-78 °C) stirring solution of
(S)-Garner’s aldehyde ent-83 (4.6 g, 20 mmol),
2,6-di-tert-butyl-4-methylpyridine (16 g, 80 mmol) and CH2Cl2 (70 mL) was
added dropwise BF3 ·Et2O (8.9 mL, 70 mmol). After stirring for 30 min at
-78°C, a solution of freshly prepared siloxyindole 7 (5.40 g, 10.0 mmol)
and CH2Cl2 (10 mL) was added dropwise. After stirring for 2 h at -78 °C
and 14 h at -50 °C, the reaction was poured into water (100 mL), the
phases were separated, and the aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2
(3x80 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried
(MgSO4) and concentrated to afford a yellowish oil. Purification of this
oil by column chromatography (20/1 to 3/1 hexanes/EtOAc) provided ent-9
(6.07 g, 92%) as a colorless foam. An analytical sample was obtained by
HPLC (85:15 hexanes-ethyl acetate, 20 mL/min): colorless foam. [α]23 D
+26.6, [α]23 577 +28.6, [α]23 546 +34.4 (c = 0.94, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Construction of Quaternary Carbon Stereocenters: High
Stereoselection in Mukaiyama Aldol Reactions of 2-Siloxyindoles with
Chiral Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
