$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure (Table 2, entry 1) : To a
suspension of 180 mg of Bi(OTf)3·4H2O (246 μmol, 1 mol %) in 20 mL of
dichloromethane was added at -70 °C, 3.18 g (27 mmol) of benzaldehyde
dimethylacetal in dichloromethane (3 mL). Then, 4.74 g (24.6 mmol) of α
-trimethylsilyloxystyrene in dichloromethane (3 mL) was added and the
reaction mixture was stirred for 15 min. After this time, water (15 mL)
was added and the products were extracted twice with 2 x 20 mL of
dichloromethane. The combined organic phases were dried (MgSO4) and
concentrated. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography on
silica gel to give product. Compound 4f. Yield 92%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bismuth(III) triflate. A water-stable equivalent of trimethylsilyl
triflate for the catalysis of Mukaiyama aldol reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Le Roux, C.; Ciliberti, L.; Laurent-Robert, H.; Laporterie, A.; Dubac, J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (1998), (11), 1249-1251

