$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Mukaiyama Aldol
Reactions Reported in Tables 1 and 2. Preparation of ent-9. To a cold
(-78 °C) stirring solution of (S)-Garner’s aldehyde ent-83 (4.6 g, 20
mmol), 2,6-di-tert-butyl-4-methylpyridine (16 g, 80 mmol) and CH2Cl2 (70
mL) was added dropwise BF3 ·Et2O (8.9 mL, 70 mmol). After stirring for 30
min at -78°C, a solution of freshly prepared siloxyindole 7 (5.40 g, 10.0
mmol) and CH2Cl2 (10 mL) was added dropwise. After stirring for 2 h at
-78 °C and 14 h at -50 °C, the reaction was poured into water (100 mL),
the phases were separated, and the aqueous phase was extracted with
CH2Cl2 (3x80 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine,
dried (MgSO4) and concentrated to afford a yellowish oil. Purification of
this oil by column chromatography (20/1 to 3/1 hexanes/EtOAc) provided
ent-9 (6.07 g, 92%) as a colorless foam. An analytical sample was
obtained by HPLC (85:15 hexanes-ethyl acetate, 20 mL/min):
3-Benzo[1,3]dioxol-5-yl-1-benzyl-3-[(2,2-dimethyl-[1,3]dioxolan-4-yl)-
hydroxymethyl]-1,3-dihydroindol-2-one (16d). According to the general
procedure, siloxyindole 13d (55 mg, 0.12 mmol) and 15 (27 mg, 0.24 mmol)
were condensed to afford a yellowish oil, which upon purification by HPLC
(82/18 hexanes/ethyl acetate; 20 mL/min) gave 16d (52 mg, 91%) as a
colorless oil. colorless oil: [α]D 27 -32.2 (c = 0.87; CHCl3); 1H NMR
(500 MHz) δ 7.36-7.41 (m, 1H), 7.23-7.33 (m, 5H), 7.21 (dt, J = 0.9 and
7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.04-7.10 (m, 2H), 6.97(dd, J = 2.0 and 8.3 Hz, 1H), 6.76
(d, J =7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.75 (d, J =8.2 Hz, 1H), 5.93 (s, 2H), 5.07 (d, J =
15.8 Hz, 1H), 4.87 (d, J =15.8 Hz, 1H), 4.64 (br d, J =6.1 Hz, 1H), 4.12
(q, J = 6.1, 1H), 3.96 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 2H), 2.95 (br s, 1H), 1.16 (s,
3H), 1.13 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz) δ 177.8, 147.3, 143.4, 135.9, 130.0,
129.2, 129.0, 128.7, 128.0, 127.5, 126.5, 122.9, 121.2, 119.7, 110.0,
109.5, 108.6, 101.5, 76.7, 67.3, 60.7, 59.9, 52.3, 44.3, 26.4, 25.3; IR
(film): 3438, 3033, 2933, 1706, 1611 cm-1; HRMS (CI) calcd for C28H28NO6
(M+H): 474.1917; found: 474.1905.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
