$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method I To a solution of OXB C or D (0.10 mmol, 1.0 eq) in butyronitrile
(0.4 mL) at -78 °C was added dropwise a solution of the corresponding
aldehyde (0.10 mmol, 1.0 eq) in butyronitrile (0.2 mL). After the
addition was completed a solution of dienolether 1 (21.9 mg, 0.14 mmol,
1.4 eq) in butyronitrile (0.2 mL) was added over 10 min using a syringe
pump. The reaction mixture was stirred for 1 h at -78 °C and quenched
with pH=7 buffer solution (0.5 mL) and slowly warmed to room temperature.
The aqueous layer was extracted with MTBE (3 x 5 mL), the combined
organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and the solvent was removed in
vacuo. To the crude product was added a mixture of THF (1.0 mL) and
hydrochloric acid (1 M, 0.1 mL) and stirred for 20 min. Saturated
NaHCO3-solution (0.5 mL) was added and the aqueous layer was extracted
with MTBE (3 x 5 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4
and the solvent was removed in vacuo. Purification by column
chromatography yielded the corresponding γ -hydroxy-α , β -unsaturated
aldehyde. Aldehyde 3 Aldehyde 3 was prepared according to method I using
OXB D. Purification by column chromatography (25% EtOAc in PE) yielded
aldehyde 3 (18.8 mg, 67 μmol, 67%) as a colorless oil. The enantiomeric
excess was determined to be 91% ee by chiral GC using Hydrodex®-PM
capillary column (100-200 °C, 1.0 °C/min) by comparison of the peaks at
82.9 min and 83.5 min. [α ]20 D = +3.8 (c = 0.4, CHCl3) Rf = 0.27 (30 %
EtOAc/PE) 1H NMR (400 MHz, C6D6) δ 9.21 (s, 1H), 5.97 - 5.95 (m, 1H),
5.95 - 5.89 (m, 1H), 3.57 - 3.50 (m, 1H), 2.06 - 1.86 (m, 2H), 1.60 -
1.51 (m, 6H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, C6D6) δ 193.8, 149.4, 148.2, 141.1, 78.9,
75.0, 34.4, 19.9, 9.4. APCI-HRMS: C9H13O2ICl [M+Cl]- calculated:
314.9649, found: 314.9655.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 91%ee, buffered solution used stage 3, Asymmetric
Vinylogous Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Vinylogous Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction of Aldehyde-Derived
Dienolates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gieseler, Marc T.; Kalesse, Markus
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(9), 2430-2432

