$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Procedure of the TFSI-H catalyzed Mukaiyama cross-aldol
reaction: To a solution of 11 (851 mg, 5.00 mmol) and
2,2-dimethoxypropane (624 mg, 6.00 mmol) in CH2Cl2 at -78 °C, was added
dropwise TFSI-H (500 L, 0.5 M solution in CH2Cl2, 0.025 mmol, 5 mol%).
After 30 min at -78 °C, the reaction mixture was poured into a sat. aq
solution of NaHCO3 and extracted with ether. The combined extracts were
washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by flash chromatography
on silica gel (Cyclohexane/EtOAc: 90/10) to give 20.18b Colorless oil,
yield 774 mg, 91%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mukaiyama cross-aldol reaction, alternative reaction conditions shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Carbon-carbon bond forming reactions by using
bistrifluoromethanesulfonimide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cossy, Janine; Lutz, Francois; Alauze, Valerie; Meyer, Christophe
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
